      "text": "EU SPIRITS REGULATION categories:\n  1. \"Gin\": juniper-flavored spirit, any method, 37.5% min\n  2. \"Distilled Gin\": redistilled with botanicals, juniper predominates\n  3. \"London Gin\" (or \"London Dry Gin\"): strictest\n     - No artificial colors/flavors\n     - No post-distillation additions except water and negligible sweetness (<0.1g/L)\n     - Must be made by distillation with botanicals\n     - Can be made anywhere in world (not geographically restricted to London)\n  4. \"Compound Gin\": essences/extracts added to neutral spirit (not redistilled)\n     -> Lower quality tier; rarely labeled as such\n```"
